<ArticleLayout title="Form 4547 after automatic enrollment" description="Understand when Form 4547 still matters for the $1,000 pilot election or a rare manual-account exception, and why claiming and activation are separate steps." verifiedAt="2026-11-27" verificationUrl={irsPilot} verificationScope="Account claims, the separate pilot election, and activation were checked against current IRS instructions and TD 10056." sourceIds={['TREASURY-TD-10056','IRS-TRUMP-ACCOUNTS','IRS-FORM-4547','IRS-FORM-4547-INSTRUCTIONS']} effective="Temporary regulations effective September 30, 2026" summary={["Check official account and pilot-election status before submitting a form.","An auto-account claim, receiving-account activation, and pilot election are separate steps.","This site does not collect or submit official account applications."]} contents={[{"id":"form-purpose","label":"What Form 4547 still does"},{"id":"check-status","label":"Step 1: check official status"},{"id":"claim","label":"Step 2: distinguish an auto-account claim from Form 4547"},{"id":"pilot","label":"Step 3: review the pilot requirements"},{"id":"manual-election","label":"Step 4: use the manual-account election only when instructed"},{"id":"activation","label":"Step 5: complete activation"},{"id":"official-links","label":"Official links"}]}>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Do not start with a duplicate form.</strong> Treasury began broad automatic enrollment on or about October 1, 2026. Check official account and pilot-election status first.</div>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Privacy boundary:</strong> this guide does not file forms, confirm payment, or collect or submit a name, SSN, date of birth, address, account number, or taxpayer information.</div>
  <h2 id="form-purpose">What Form 4547 still does</h2>
  <p>Check the <a href={irsAccounts}>IRS instructions for claiming an automatically opened account</a>. That claim does not require Form 4547. For an eligible child, follow the <a href={irsAccounts}>IRS steps to elect the separate $1,000 pilot contribution on Form 4547</a>, even if Treasury opened the account automatically.</p>
  <p>If the official record confirms there is no account or prior election, see the <a href="https://www.irs.gov/forms-pubs/about-form-4547">IRS guidance on using Form 4547 to elect an initial account</a> and <a href={temporaryRule}>TD 10056 for the no-prior-election requirement</a>.</p>
  <h2 id="check-status">Step 1: check official status</h2>
  <p>Start at <a href={portal}>TrumpAccounts.gov</a>. Determine whether Treasury has established an auto account, whether someone previously made an account election, and whether a pilot election is pending or processed. An unknown or pending status should be resolved before another submission.</p>
  <h2 id="claim">Step 2: distinguish an auto-account claim from Form 4547</h2>
  <p>Under <a href={temporaryRule}>TD 10056</a>, a guardian or legal custodian with authority under state law to manage the beneficiary’s property or financial affairs, or a beneficiary with legal capacity, may use Treasury’s electronic claim process. The claimant must verify identity and authority and complete required consents. A family relationship alone may be insufficient.</p>
  <h2 id="pilot">Step 3: review the pilot requirements</h2>
  <p>Review the <a href={irsPilot}>IRS Form 4547 pilot-election instructions</a> before filing.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The child generally must be a U.S. citizen born from January 1, 2025 through December 31, 2028.</li>
    <li>The child must have an employment-valid SSN issued before the election and meet the account age requirement.</li>
    <li>The person making the pilot election must expect the child to be their qualifying child for the election year.</li>
    <li>Check whether an earlier pilot election was processed; treat a merely submitted election as pending until official status is known.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 id="manual-election">Step 4: use the manual-account election only when instructed</h2>
  <p>If the IRS confirms that no account or prior election exists, follow the current instructions to determine whether a rare manual Form 4547 account election is appropriate. Do not rely on pre-auto-enrollment articles as the current default process.</p>
  <h2 id="activation">Step 5: complete activation</h2>
  <p><a href={temporaryRule}>TD 10056 requires activation of the receiving account</a> after a claim. Follow the trustee’s instructions for the account agreement and confirm that the receiving account is ready before arranging family or employer deposits.</p>
  <p><a class="button" href="/tools/trump-account-eligibility-checker/">Run the private next-step check</a></p>
